<section class="sec"><div class="wrap"><div class="guide-grid" data-stagger><article class="guide rv"><a class="ph" href="/learning-center/wisconsin-appraisal-clause-guide/" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/assets/img/photos/paperwork.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/paperwork-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/paperwork.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 400px" width="1024" height="680" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></a><div class="bd"><span class="meta">Aug 11, 2026 · 7 min read</span><h2><a href="/learning-center/wisconsin-appraisal-clause-guide/">Reading the Appraisal Clause in Your Wisconsin Property Policy</a></h2><p>The appraisal clause is short, but each phrase shapes how a dispute plays out. Here’s how to read the version in your Wisconsin policy.</p><a class="arrow-link" href="/learning-center/wisconsin-appraisal-clause-guide/">Read the guide <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></div></article><article class="guide rv"><a class="ph" href="/learning-center/ice-dam-insurance-claims/" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/assets/img/photos/icicles.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/icicles-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/icicles.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 400px" width="1024" height="685" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></a><div class="bd"><span class="meta">Aug 27, 2026 · 7 min read</span><h2><a href="/learning-center/ice-dam-insurance-claims/">Ice Dam Insurance Claims in Wisconsin: What’s Usually Covered and How to Document It</a></h2><p>Ice dams are a fact of Wisconsin winters. Here’s how coverage typically works, where claims get disputed and how to build a strong file.</p><a class="arrow-link" href="/learning-center/ice-dam-insurance-claims/">Read the guide <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></div></article><article class="guide rv"><a class="ph" href="/learning-center/hail-claim-photo-checklist/" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/assets/img/photos/roof-tarp.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/roof-tarp-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/roof-tarp.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 400px" width="1024" height="765" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></a><div class="bd"><span class="meta">Sep 15, 2026 · 6 min read</span><h2><a href="/learning-center/hail-claim-photo-checklist/">Hail Claim Photo Checklist: Documenting Damage After a Wisconsin Storm</a></h2><p>Good photos taken soon after a storm are the backbone of a hail claim. Use this checklist to document what an adjuster or appraiser will need.</p><a class="arrow-link" href="/learning-center/hail-claim-photo-checklist/">Read the guide <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></div></article><article class="guide rv"><a class="ph" href="/learning-center/sewer-backup-vs-flood-coverage/" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/assets/img/photos/ceiling-water.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/ceiling-water-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/ceiling-water.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 400px" width="1024" height="683" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></a><div class="bd"><span class="meta">Oct 2, 2026 · 8 min read</span><h2><a href="/learning-center/sewer-backup-vs-flood-coverage/">Sewer Backup vs. Flood Coverage: How Wisconsin Basement Water Claims Differ</a></h2><p>A wet basement can fall under three very different coverages, or none. Here’s a cautious overview of how they usually differ.</p><a class="arrow-link" href="/learning-center/sewer-backup-vs-flood-coverage/">Read the guide <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></div></article><article class="guide rv"><a class="ph" href="/learning-center/derecho-straight-line-wind-claims/" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/assets/img/photos/wind-damage.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/wind-damage-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/wind-damage.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 400px" width="1024" height="681" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></a><div class="bd"><span class="meta">Oct 20, 2026 · 7 min read</span><h2><a href="/learning-center/derecho-straight-line-wind-claims/">Derecho and Straight-Line Wind Claims: Why They Get Disputed and How to Scope Them</a></h2><p>Derechos can damage thousands of properties in a single day. Here’s why wind claims get contested and how a thorough scope helps.</p><a class="arrow-link" href="/learning-center/derecho-straight-line-wind-claims/">Read the guide <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></div></article><article class="guide rv"><a class="ph" href="/learning-center/matching-siding-and-shingles/" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/assets/img/photos/roof-shingles.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/roof-shingles-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/roof-shingles.webp 960w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 400px" width="960" height="526" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></a><div class="bd"><span class="meta">Nov 5, 2026 · 7 min read</span><h2><a href="/learning-center/matching-siding-and-shingles/">Matching Siding and Shingles After a Claim: Discontinued Materials and Uniform Appearance</a></h2><p>When replacement siding or shingles don’t match, a small repair can leave a patchwork. 